ve Bayes Hidden-Markov Model to detect and accurately map copy number variation using SNP genotyping data</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res.</source><year>2007</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>2013</fpage><lpage>2025</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17341461</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>FS</given-names></name><name><surname>Barker</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mapping the cancer genome. Pinpointing the genes involved in cancer will help chart a new course across the complex landscape of human malignancies</article-title><source>Sci. Am.</source><year>2007</year><volume>296</volume><fpage>50</fpage><lpage>57</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17348159</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>de Leeuw</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Comprehensive whole genome array CGH profiling of mantle cell lymphoma model genomes</article-title><source>Hum. Mol. Genet.</source><year>2004</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>1827</fpage><lpage>1837</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15229187</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dempster</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Maximum likelihood from incomplete data via the EM algorithm</article-title><source>J. R. Stat. Soci. Ser. B</source><year>1977</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>38</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diskin</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>STAC: A method for testing the significance of DNA copy number aberrations across multiple array-CGH experiments</article-title><source>Genome Res.</source><year>2006</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>1149</fpage><lpage>1158</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16899652</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gilks</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><source>Markov Chain Monte Carlo in Practice.</source><year>1996</year><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Chapman &#x00026; Hall</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>H&#x000f6;glund</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Identification of cytogenetic subgroups and karyotypic pathways of clonal evolution in follicular lymphomas</article-title><source>Genes Chromosomes Cancer</source><year>2004</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>195</fpage><lpage>204</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14732921</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Idbaih</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>BAC array CGH distinguishes mutually exclusive alterations that define clinicogenetic subtypes of gliomas</article-title><source>Int. J. Cancer</source><year>2008</year><volume>122</volume><fpage>1778</fpage><lpage>1786</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18076069</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ishkanian</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A tiling resolution DNA microarray with complete coverage of the human genome</article-title><source>Nat. Genet.</source><year>2004</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>299</fpage><lpage>303</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14981516</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Deletion in chromosome 17p12 and gains in chromosome 9q33.3 by array comparative hybridization are associated with R-CHOP treatment failure in patients with diffuse large B cell lymphoma</article-title><source>Blood</source><year>2008</year><volume>111</volume><fpage>a477</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Khalique</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Genetic intra-tumour heterogeneity in epithelial ovarian cancer and its implications for molecular diagnosis of tumours</article-title><source>J. Pathol.</source><year>2007</year><volume>211</volume><fpage>286</fpage><lpage>295</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17154249</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Klijn</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Identification of cancer genes using a statistical framework for multiexperiment analysis of nondiscretized array CGH data</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res.</source><year>2008</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>e13</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18187509</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Law</surname><given-names>MHC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Simultaneous Feature selection and clustering using mixture models</article-title><source>IEEE Trans. Pattern Anal. Mach. Intell.</source><year>2004</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>1154</fpage><lpage>1166</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15742891</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Michels</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>ArrayCGH-based classification of neuroblastoma into genomic subgroups</article-title><source>Genes Chromosomes Cancer</source><year>2007</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>1098</fpage><lpage>1108</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17823929</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Perou</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Molecular portraits of human breast tumours</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2000</year><volume>406</volume><fpage>747</fpage><lpage>752</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10963602</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pinkel</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Albertson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Array comparative genomic hybridization and its applications in cancer</article-title><source>Nat. Genet.</source><year>2005</year><volume>37</volume><issue>Suppl</issue><fpage>11</fpage><lpage>17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15624015</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Raftery</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Dean</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Variable selection for model-based clustering</article-title><source>J. Am. Stat. Assoc.</source><year>2006</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>168</fpage><lpage>178</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rouveirol</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Computation of recurrent minimal genomic alterations from array-CGH data</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><year>2006</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>849</fpage><lpage>856</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16434445</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scharpf</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Hidden Markov models for the assessment of chromosomal alterations using high-throughput SNP arrays</article-title><source>Ann. Appl. Stat.</source><year>2008</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>687</fpage><lpage>713</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shah</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Integrating copy number polymorphisms into array CGH analysis using a robust HMM</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><year>2006</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>431</fpage><lpage>439</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shah</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Modeling recurrent DNA copy number alterations in array CGH data</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><year>2007</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>450</fpage><lpage>458</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17150994</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sorlie</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular portraits of breast cancer: tumour subtypes as distinct disease entities</article-title><source>Eur. J. Cancer</source><year>2004</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>2667</fpage><lpage>2675</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15571950</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B32"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tan</surname><given-names>P-N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><source>Introduction to Data Mining.</source><year>2005</year><edition>First</edition><publisher-loc>Boston, MA, USA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Addison-Wesley Longman Publishing Co., Inc.</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B33"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tonon</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>High-resolution genomic profiles of human lung cancer</article-title><source>Proc. Natl Acad. Sci. USA</source><year>2005</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>9625</fpage><lpage>9630</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15983384</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B34"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van der Laan</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A new partitioning around medoids algorithm</article-title><source>J. Stat. Comput. Simul.</source><year>2003</year><volume>73</volume><fpage>575</fpage><lpage>584</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B35"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van Wieringen</surname><given-names>WN</given-names></name><name><surname>van de</surname><given-names>Wiel,MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nonparametric testing for DNA copy number induced differential mRNA gene expression</article-title><source>Biometrics</source><year>2008</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>484</fpage><lpage>500</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B36"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wright</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A gene expression-based method to diagnose clinically distinct subgroups of diffuse large b cell lymphoma</article-title><source>Proc. Natl Acad. Sci. USA</source><year>2003</year><volume>100</volume><fpage>9991</fpage><lpage>9996</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12900505</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>